  {
   "key": "similar",
   "title": "Diseases that look or share biology like CLN2",
   "text": "CLN3 is a disease with similar symptoms, different cause compared to CLN2; according to HPO, both conditions can include myoclonus, meaning sudden muscle jerks [E7982300, E0282bf7]. According to HPO, both CLN2 and CLN3 can cause progressive loss of vision over time [E24d0838, Ece5a0d1]. According to HPO, both can also show an undetectable electroretinogram, which is a test that checks how the eye reacts to light [E692fe55, E505ff82].",
   "citations": [
