  {
   "key": "what_exists",
   "title": "Groups, researchers, and trials connected to CLN2",
   "text": "A paper reports that Taylor's Tale, a patient group based in the United States, is linked to CLN2 [E8e670ee]. A paper reports that the Batten Disease Support and Research Association keeps up-to-date information on every known form of Batten disease [E613fcb3]. According to NIH RePORTER, NIH NICHD and NIH NINDS fund several research grants that study CLN2, including work connected to Erika Augustine, Jill M Weimer, Anil B Mukherjee, and Jonathan D Cooper [Eba9be50, Eccc3ac9, E055be57, E53f8887, E979376d, E215c22c, Ec74b030, E6d64cb3, E574608d, Ed3a744a]. We matched by name that Jonathan D Cooper also authored a paper about chronic oral cannabidiol in a mouse model of CLN2 disease [Ee1b95c1]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, BioMarin Pharmaceutical runs an observational study of Cerliponase Alfa for CLN2 that is active but not recruiting, with a site in the United States [E6239b0d, E88ec7f7, E92a7022, Ed82970f]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, David L Rogers, MD runs a trial giving Cerliponase Alfa directly into the eye to look at retinal disease progression in children with CLN2, which is active but not recruiting, with a site in the United States [E63570b1, E01eb273, E63f5644, E79e2025]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, Polaryx Therapeutics runs a trial testing PLX-200 for children with CLN2 that is not yet recruiting [E2aaf128, E12fae6f, E0fb2a07]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, The Charlotte and Gwenyth Gray Foundation runs a gene therapy trial that studies CLN2, testing scAAV9.CB.CLN6, which is not yet recruiting, with a site in the United States [E5406472, E54b7767, E94e3acf, Eea9930a]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, Albert Einstein College of Medicine runs a newborn screening study called ScreenPlus that includes CLN2 and is enrolling by invitation, with a site in the United States [E2523361, E17af82a, Ec294d25].",
